narrative:
## Inner Blocks and Borrow Control

Nested scopes (blocks within blocks) give you fine-grained control over variable lifetimes and borrow durations.

### Creating Inner Scopes

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let x = 1;
  {  // inner scope 1
    let y = 2;
    {  // inner scope 2
      let z = 3;
      // can access x, y, z
    }  // z dropped
    // can access x, y
  }  // y dropped
  // can access x only
  return x;
}
```

### Borrow Control with Nested Scopes

```xiom
var data = Vec[Int]();
data.push(1);

// First modification
{
  let m = &mut data;
  m.push(2);
}

// Read
let len = data.len();

// Second modification
{
  let m = &mut data;
  m.push(3);
}

return data.len();  // 3
```

### Pattern: Scope for Temporary Mutations

```xiom
fn process_in_batches(v: &mut Vec[Int]) -> Unit {
  {
    // batch 1
    v.push(1); v.push(2); v.push(3);
  }
  let count = v.len();  // read
  {
    // batch 2
    v.push(4); v.push(5);
  }
}
```

### Variable Shadowing

Inner scopes can shadow (redeclare) outer variables:

```xiom
let x = 5;
{
  let x = x * 2;  // inner x = 10, outer x unchanged
  io.println(x);   // prints 10
}
io.println(x);     // prints 5 — outer x unchanged
```

